---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, withBase } from '../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="The only blog dedicated to medicine and cocktails, written by a practicing family physician.">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 44rem">
    <p class="kicker" style="color: var(--amber)">The masthead</p>
    <h1 style="font-family: var(--serif-display); font-size: clamp(2rem,5vw,3.2rem); letter-spacing:-0.03em; margin: 0 0 0.8rem;">About</h1>
    <div class="prose" style="margin: 0; padding: 0; max-width: none">
      <p>
        This is the only blog dedicated to medicine and cocktails. That is not a branding exercise.
        It is simply what the work and the evenings look like.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am a practicing family physician. In clinic I write notes, argue with electronic records,
        sit with patients, and try to practice good medicine in a system that often makes that harder
        than it should be. After hours — and sometimes because of those hours — I think about bourbon,
        rye, barrel-aging, ice, and the small ceremonies that make a drink worth having.
      </p>
      <p>
        The pieces here are candid. Clinic life, insurance enrollment, waiting rooms, bad sazeracs,
        a first trip down the Kentucky Bourbon Trail, a car that almost ran me over in my own garage.
        I write as <strong>{SITE.author}</strong>. No hospital press office, no invented credentials.
        If a story involves a patient, the details are handled the way they should be: enough to tell
        the truth, not enough to point at a person.
      </p>
      <p>
        I started this journal in 2017 because the two subjects kept colliding — a bottle of Jameson
        off a cabinet, a Medicare question in November, a barrel of Creole cocktail going slightly
        wrong. They still do.
      </p>
      <p>
        Essays have a comments box. Your email is required and is never published;
        nothing appears until I approve it. You can also write on X at
        <a href={SITE.twitter} rel="me noopener">{SITE.twitterHandle}</a>.
        Subscribe via <a href={withBase('rss.xml')}>RSS</a>.
        There is no public email address and no contact form. Linking is welcome; republishing is not.
      </p>
      <p><em>{SITE.copyright}</em></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
